WHAT: Adds LoadStore and CheckedArithElim to the post-dead-arg cleanup passes.

WHY: After dead argument elimination creates new opportunities, running
LoadStore (object load/store optimization) and CheckedArithElim (checked
arithmetic elimination) might catch patterns that were previously hidden.

GAS IMPACT: None on rosetta contracts.

TEAM NOTES: Like step 5, this is theoretically sound but hits diminishing
returns. The stubborn contracts (math, escrow, AMM) have fundamental patterns
that require different solutions — not more optimizer passes on the same IR.
Steps 3-6 as a group show that inliner tuning and pipeline expansion have
a ceiling. The next wins require changing what the compiler generates (Fe
lowering) or how it schedules instructions (stackifier).
